; tests/gen-conformance-band.fk — a page of generated code, 110 questions, two
; real toolchains that share no code with each other or with Form, the body's
; own Python model reading and running the Python page, and the body itself
; running the Form program the graph wrote.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM + GO — host-exec binds on go and fkwu (pf-arm-mask 9, probed 2026-09-03; rust/ts do not bind it). The Python model's chain carries BML, which a sibling reads only through validate.sh's lowering; the verdict below stands on fkwu. Running a real
; toolchain is the entire point. Nothing here walks a recipe: Form is judged by
; fkwu compiling and running the text the generator wrote, so the chain holds
; no arm-specific door beyond host-exec, resolves clean and exits 0.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/json.fk form-stdlib/cache.fk form-stdlib/form-ontology-bp.fk form-stdlib/engine.fk form-stdlib/compiler.fk form-stdlib/source-compiler.fk form-stdlib/grammars/python-bmf.fk form-stdlib/python-bmf-lift.fk form-stdlib/python-bmf-eval.fk cognition/language-neutral-symbol-identity.fk cognition/steiner-neutral-kernel.fk cognition/gen-neutral-code.fk cognition/gen-query-flow.fk cognition/gen-conformance.fk
;
; Verdict 2097151 — twenty-one readings:
;   three of the four languages have a page runner — node, go, and the
;     body's own Python model                                               1
;   and ONE has none — Form, which refuses the page (16384); it is never
;     counted as a page pass                                                2
;   every page-judged language matches the graph, case for case             4
;   python: a page emitted, read and run by the body's own Python model
;     (python-bmf lift + eval on fkwu), every answer compared               8
;   javascript: emitted, run by node                                       16
;   go: emitted, compiled and run by go                                    32
;   NO LANGUAGE IS LEFT UNJUDGED: node and go on the page, the body's
;     Python model on the page, and Form by fkwu — found at the checkout
;     root — on the program it speaks                                      64
;
;   THE SWEEP, sized from the graph rather than from a typed number:
;   more than 105 cases — every (shape, relation, key) triple some
;     fact makes answerable, deduplicated, plus the join cases            128
;   and every case has an answering row, so this is not a wall of
;     agreeing zeros                                                      256
;   and more than ten are MULTI-MATCH — the only cases that test
;     first-match order at all                                            512
;
;   THE CHECK NOBODY AUTHORED: summing a count shape over every distinct
;     key for a relation equals the number of facts carrying it. A
;     property of counting, true of any correct implementation. A
;     swapped column leaves every single answer plausible and breaks
;     this sum — the one failure the sweep cannot see, because a
;     swapped column would be swapped in the reference too              1024
;
;   A PAGE OF CODE, measured on the emitted text:
;   python over 75 lines                                                2048
;   javascript over 75 lines                                            4096
;   go over 75 lines                                                    8192
;   and Form REFUSES the page and emits nothing. This reading has been
;     wrong twice: first "Form carries no slet row" (inference — it
;     does), then "Form renders the whole page" (it rendered TEXT that
;     overflowed the value stack when run, because its `ret` and `sif`
;     rows discarded every early exit). Both passed green, because
;     Form had no runner then and the reading measured characters.
;     The counterfeit rows are gone; its honest lane is the
;     expression form, which the Form judge runs                       16384
;
;   THE DELTA WITNESS: no single output can prove it was generated rather
;     than typed. What a template cannot do is track a predicted change in
;     its input. Add one fact and exactly one count answer rises by
;     exactly one                                                        32768
;   while 108 of the other 109 stay identical — not 109, because the
;     injected row has subject == object, so the object-column count for
;     the same key moves too. The second mover is the delta landing where
;     the semantics say it should                                        65536
;
;   THE JOIN: four of the thirty-six possible relation pairs actually
;     chain — some fact's object under r1 is some fact's subject under
;     r2 — read from the graph rather than chosen. The emitted code is
;     two recursions of five and three parameters, which no row of a
;     (match-column, mode, result-column) table can be                  131072
;
;   THE FORM JUDGE — the body runs what the graph wrote. The generator
;     renders the count program for a concept as Form source (505
;     characters, one term per has-member fact), the checkout's fkwu
;     compiles and runs it, and what it prints, with exit status 0,
;     must equal the graph read directly:
;   the threefold soul — fkwu prints 3                                  262144
;   the fourfold being — fkwu prints 4                                  524288
;   eurythmy, a concept with no members — fkwu prints 0; its program is
;     the same full chain, every term comparing against a concept no
;     fact names                                                       1048576
(do
    (gcf-check))
